    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0340" n="1074" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1074"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Breckinridge.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic">May 16,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 57.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a copy of a dispatch from our
                    minister at Peking,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d287-f1"/> stating that the Russian
                    minister at that capital had, under the regulations of his Government, declined
                    to issue a passport or some official paper to certain American missionaries
                    residing at Kalgan, in China, enabling them to take temporary refuge in Russian
                    territory, in case the outbreak of an insurrection in China imperiled their
                    lives.</p>
                <p>You may take occasion to inquire whether the Russian regulations against the
                    residence or travel of foreign ecclesiastics or missionaries in Siberia are as
                    strict as Count Cassini interprets them to be, even to the inhospitable degree
                    of denying shelter to citizens of a friendly State whose lives might be
                    imperiled.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
